    "narrative": "The LawDog lineup is headlined by **Jonathan Aranda** (68.94) and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (66.22), our two most reliable anchors today. **Jonathan Aranda** draws a favorable matchup against Bieber, where the combination of a weak 5.10 xERA and a beneficial platoon split boosts his output significantly. Similarly, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains a plug-and-play asset despite a tougher opponent in Bradley; his high base projection is buoyed by the aggressive pursuit of stolen bases, as the matchup against a slower-to-the-plate starter offers a tactical advantage for him to manufacture value. **Geraldo Perdomo** also clears the 60.0 threshold, providing steady production from the #2 spot against McGreevy, making him an efficient play to maximize our total game caps.\n\n**Masyn Winn** and **Gleyber Torres** occupy the middle of our scoring distribution, though their paths to relevance differ. **Masyn Winn** (55.53) provides crucial SB utility, benefiting from a high-efficiency environment against Pfaadt, whereas **Gleyber Torres** (59.11) sees his score tethered by a challenging platoon split against Dobnak. Our most difficult decision was keeping **Gavin Sheets** on the bench. He finished with a 36.02, falling well below our 40.0 floor; despite some decent park factors, the significant SP skill of Sale effectively neutralized his outlook, leading to a disciplined decision to preserve our limited game caps for more favorable matchups.\n\nWe are navigating a quiet day for the broader squad, with key contributors like **Bryce Harper**, **Cal Raleigh**, **Lawrence Butler**, **Yainer Diaz**, **Tyler Freeman**, **Will Smith**, **Taylor Ward**, **Matt Chapman**, **Daulton Varsho**, **Luis Arraez**, **Dylan Beavers**, **JJ Bleday**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Zack Gelof**, **Alex Freeland**, **Kyle Karros**, and **Drew Gilbert** all sidelined due to team off-days. With **Ryan Waldschmidt** (46.10) rounding out the active starters, we are counting on his positional depth to contribute, though his low spot in the batting order limits his ceiling. We will monitor lineup updates closely to ensure no late-scratch risks emerge, but for now, the internal models indicate a high-floor day for the active roster.",
